 "text": "..title\nAn ordinance authorizing the acquisition of certain right-of-way easements, drainage easements, temporary construction easements and property rights by negotiation or condemnation for use in public projects of the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County, acting by and through the Nashville Department of Transportation and Multimodal Infrastructure (“NDOT”), for purposes of Highway 100 sidewalk improvements, NDOT Project Number 2023-093. (Proposal No. 2026M-046AG-001).\n..body\nWHEREAS, NDOT seeks to acquire right-of-way easements, temporary construction easements, and property rights for purposes of its sidewalk improvement project on Highway 100, from Highway 100 west of Collins Road to Highway 100 east of Old Harding Pike, NDOT Project Number 2023-093, Proposal No. 2026M-046AG-001 (“the Project”); and,\nWHEREAS, the right-of-way easements, temporary construction easements and property rights associated with the Project are located on the property described in Exhibit 1, attached hereto and incorporated by reference; and, \nWHEREAS, the easements and property rights associated with the Project are further described in NDOT’s plans on file for the Project, which are incorporated by reference; and,\nWHEREAS, it is in the public interest that right-of-way easements, drainage easements, temporary construction easements, and property rights be acquired by the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County, for use in public project referenced herein; and,\nWHEREAS, it is in the best interest of the Metropolitan Government that this construction be carried out.\nNOW, THEREFORE BE IT ENACTED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.    \tThe Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County, by and through the Director of Public Property Administration, is hereby authorized to acquire, by negotiation or condemnation, right-of-way easement and property rights for use in the Nashville Department of Transportation and Multimodal Infrastructure (“NDOT”) Highway 100 sidewalk improvements project, from Highway 100 west of Collins Road to Highway 100 east of Old Harding Pike, NDOT Project No. 2023-093, Proposal No. 2026M-046AG-001 (“the Project”), the same being for a public purpose and the public convenience requiring it. \nSection 2.    The easements and property rights to be acquired for the Project are located on the property described in Exhibit 1, attached hereto and incorporated by reference herein, and described in NDOT’s plans on file for the Project, which are incorporated by reference herein.\nSection 3.    \tThe Director of Public Property Administration is hereby authorized and directed, to acquire by negotiation or, if necessary, to take and appropriate by condemnation proceedings the interests in real property described herein in the name of the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County for use in the public project referenced herein.\nSection 4.    \tAll necessary and incidental costs of the right-of-way easements and property rights herein authorized to be acquired shall be paid from funds authorized from Fund No. 40023 and Business Unit No. 42402023.\nSection 5.\tAmendments to this legislation shall be approved by resolution. \nSection 6.    \tThis ordinance shall take effect from and after its final passage, the welfare of the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it. \n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis ordinance authorizes NDOT and the Director of Public Property to acquire right-of-way easements, temporary construction easements and property rights across five tracts on Highway 100, from Highway 100 west of Collins Road to Highway 100 east of Old Harding Pike. These acquisitions shall be used for rights-of-way, drainage easements, and construction easements related to sidewalk improvements on Highway 100. \n\nThis ordinance has been approved by the Planning Commission. Future amendments to this ordinance may be approved by resolution.\n\n"
